                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played for 2.8 hours to be exact and completed this game. I'm not sure but I believe that .4 of those hours were spent smoking with my wife while the game was running in the background. It was bought for 4 dollars and obviously tax and that equals something like $1.54 per hour of play and I kind of wish that I had just YouTubed the ending of this game and called it a day. I by no means was speed running this game and am extremely disappointed. It is just long enough that you won't be getting a refund.  This feels like this is some persons college mid term project and they just went ahead and released it here on steam in attempt to cash in on your desire to find that next Limbo game. IT'S NOT THAT.\r\n\r\nI'm going to spoil the game for you just so your mad enough not to buy it. You Run through puzzles that aren't puzzles what so ever. I mean, you could tell that there were suppose to be some form of puzzles but there wasn't any puzzles because... WHO THE FK KNOWS?  You NEVER get any new powers, you never grow up, you never feel like you achieved anything, The background never changes any color, patterns, imagery and even when walking through a dark cave, you can still tell your literally in the same environment. It's about as equivalent as you walking across the street to your mailbox. Just 2 hours of it. After you beat the game they say \"thanks and special thanks\" to a list of people (how it's a list this long of people is mind numbing honestly) but then get this.... They have the nerve to say thanks to \"their patient fans\".... WHO? There's nothing to be patient for. There is no substance to this game other than walk right, so who the hell was sweating these people sooo bad that they needed to thank \"patient fans\". These people put in the least amount of effort for nothing more than a \"walk forward\", 2.8 hour story. Once you get to the END you play a match of tennis with some magic rat, beat him and save your boyfriend/ girlfriend and from what me and my wife could tell, they hump it out and then the credits roll. IF you're thinking \"well, now I'm curious to see these things hump\", let me tell you, it isn't anything like I just made it sound. BUT that's the game.  If you buy this game you will hate yourself because you will WISH that  it was something that it's not.\r\n\r\n I'm legit upset because I was excited to play this. It's charm lasted for 20 minutes but runs out just as quickly. Half way through I found myself hoping that I beat it soon so I could move on to the next backlog title. Because this is ultimately one of those BS Ps plus titles  that playstation would dump on you for free, you'd add it to your backlog, never touch it and then your subscription would run out and you'd be like \"oh well, the titles were crap anyways\". It's 2. something hours long. \r\n\r\nI'm willing to bet right now that my review here will offer more entertainment value than the entirety of this game.  I believe this game could have been made on ps4 title Dreams.\r\n\r\n",
